{
  "title": "Lists — Ordered Containers",
  "subtitle": "Storing Sequences with Square Brackets & 0-Based Indexing",
  "topic": "7.1 • LISTS BASICS",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      7.1 • Data Collections\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Python <hlt>Lists</hlt>\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Instead of creating 10 separate variables, a <strong>List</strong> holds multiple values in an ordered sequence inside square brackets <code>[ ]</code>!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"lesson-ref-card\">\n    <div class=\"lesson-ref-header\">\n      <span class=\"ref-badge\">PREVIOUS KNOWLEDGE</span>\n      <span class=\"lesson-ref-title\">Connecting to Earlier Concepts</span>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lesson-ref-desc\">\n      In Lesson 3, we stored single values in boxes. A List is like an organized egg carton with numbered slots for multiple values!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=3&sub=1&ref_from=1_8_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Variables & Boxes (Lesson 3.1) →</a>\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=6&sub=3&ref_from=1_8_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: for Loops over Collections (Lesson 6.1) →</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Indexing Rules\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      0-Based & Negative Indexing\n    </h2>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      fruits = [<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Apple\"</span>, <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Banana\"</span>, <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Cherry\"</span>]<br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(fruits[<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">0</span>])   <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># First item: \"Apple\"</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(fruits[<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">1</span>])   <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Second item: \"Banana\"</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(fruits[-<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">1</span>])  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Last item: \"Cherry\"</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">len</span>(fruits)) <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Length: 3</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}